# Development guide

## Quickstart

```bash
gh repo clone {{ github_owner }}/{{ project_name }}
cd {{ project_name }}

# Install uv
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh

# Install dependencies. uv reads .python-version to pick the interpreter for .venv.
uv sync --all-groups --all-extras

# Install pre-commit hooks if you plan to modify the code
uv run pre-commit install
{%- if use_docker %}

# Docker Compose is required for the local stack and for database tests.
docker compose version
{%- endif %}
```
{%- if use_docker %}

### Running the application

```bash
mkdir -p logs
LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG IMAGE_TAG=local PULL_POLICY=never docker compose up --build
{%- if use_fastapi %}
curl http://localhost:8080/health
{%- endif %}
```

Stop with `docker compose down`; add `-v` to drop the Postgres volume and start from scratch.

> **After a schema change, reset the volume.** `create_all` only creates *missing* tables and
> enum types; it never `ALTER`s an existing schema. Run `docker compose down -v` before the
> next `up`, otherwise the stale schema persists in the `pgdata` volume.
{%- endif %}

## Creating commits and pull requests

### Branch naming

Use the pattern `username/two-four-word-description`, for example `{{ github_owner }}/add-rate-limiting`.

### Commit messages

Follow Conventional Commits (`conventionalcommits.org`):

```txt
<type>(scope): <subject>
```

Valid types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `chore`, `docs`, `test`, `ci`, `style`, `perf`, `build`.
Write the subject in imperative mood ("add", "fix", "remove", not "added", "fixes", "removed").
Keep the first line under 50 characters and the full message under 100 words.

```txt
feat(api): add rate limiting
fix(worker): retry on transient timeouts
docs(readme): update local setup instructions
```

### Pre-commit hooks

`uv run pre-commit install` registers the hooks in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`. CI runs the same
hooks and enforces changed-line coverage (below).

Some hooks (ruff) modify files in place. The commit then aborts because the working tree changed
after staging; re-add and commit again:

```bash
git add -u
git commit
```

Do not skip hooks with `--no-verify`. If a hook fails and you do not understand why, ask before
bypassing it.

### Pull requests

Follow `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`. Keep PRs small; see [git-and-small-prs.md](git-and-small-prs.md).

## Running the tests

Test files live next to the code they cover and end with `*_test.py`, never `test_*.py`.

```bash
# Default suite (excludes integration and live tests)
uv run pytest -m "not integration and not live"

# Coverage command used by pre-commit and CI
uv run pytest -m "not integration and not live" --cov --cov-report=xml

# Changed-line coverage against main (CI requires at least 80%)
uv run diff-cover coverage.xml --compare-branch=origin/main --fail-under=80

# Everything
uv run pytest
```

## Toolchain

| Tool | Role |
|---|---|
| `uv` | Dependency resolution, virtualenv, Python version (`.python-version`), lockfile (`uv.lock`, committed) |
| `ruff` | Lint (`select = ["ALL"]` with a commented ignore list) and format |
| `mypy` + `basedpyright` | Two type checkers; each catches what the other misses |
| `pyrefly` | Fast type checking in the editor (`pyrefly.toml`) |
| `bandit`, `pip-audit` | Security lint and dependency vulnerability audit |
| `pytest`, `pytest-cov`, `diff-cover` | Tests and changed-line coverage gate |
| `pre-commit` | Runs all of the above before each commit and in CI |
{%- if use_docker %}
| `docker compose` | Local stack; `docker-compose.override.yaml` for per-machine overrides |
{%- endif %}

`pyproject.toml` configures every tool. Runtime dependencies live under `[project.dependencies]`,
development tools under `[dependency-groups.dev]`.
{%- if use_docker %}

### Container image

The Dockerfile declares the uv image as a build stage so Dependabot can update it, installs
with `uv sync --frozen --no-dev` from the committed lockfile, and runs as a non-root user. The
`IMAGE_VERSION` build arg defaults to `project.version`; the `check-container-version` hook
keeps the two equal, and CI overrides it with
`<project-version>-dev.<run-number>.<attempt>+g<seven-character-commit>`.
{%- endif %}
